{
  "id": "funnel_p_exact_binomial",
  "reference": "Physician-level proportions (14 physicians, 18-220 patients, ~14.5% event rate) on a p funnel: exact binomial limits, Spiegelhalter 2005 Appendix A.1.1. At n = 18 the 99.8% upper limit is 0.4812 against a 3-sigma value of 0.394, and the lower limit is 0, not a clipped negative. The published estimator finds over-dispersion (phi-hat = 1.472172, tau-hat = 0.028977), which an unadjusted funnel reports but does not apply. Cross-checked against an independent numpy + scipy.stats implementation of the whole chain (center line, Pearson residuals, winsorizing, method-of-moments tau^2, and the interpolated quantile of scipy's distribution) to ~1e-11. Upper contours sit at the exact one-sided test's boundary, one count beyond the interpolated quantile, so a point is beyond either line exactly when its exact p-value is below that line's tail probability (docs/methods.md \u00a74.1).",
